#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ft-voiced: Frametop Voice, local dictation and wake words (frametop-voice.service).

One PipeWire capture stream (pw-record) feeds two consumers:
  * dictation: push-to-talk -> record -> the recognizer, once the recording is over -> the input
    relay types the text where typing goes
  * wake word: sherpa-onnx keyword spotter -> capture the spoken command -> the recognizer ->
    a voice command (voice_commands.py), or the command hook and event subscribers

Nothing is typed while you talk: the pill in the headset (notice.py) shows that it listens, then
that it's typing. The recognizer hears the whole recording at once, with its silences cut out
(the VAD), which is what makes it accurate; a long one goes to it in pieces cut at pauses while
it's still being made, so the wait after the release stays a second or two.

Push-to-talk comes from the input relay (a key combination or mouse button with the dictate or
dictate_hold action: "toggle|start|stop|cancel <source> [quiet]" on @frametop_voice, taken only
from this user; quiet: no cancel tone) and from Frame controller buttons, read from SteamVR's web
socket (input/vrws.py), so they still do what they do in games. Text goes to the relay as "type
TEXT" on @frametop_relay, any language's characters: it types them with the keys of the desktop's
keyboard layout, and only while no modifier is held, so letters never turn into shortcuts.

The language ("language" in the settings) picks the recognizer (voice_settings.engine_for):
Parakeet on the CPU (voice_engine.py) for the 25 languages it knows, English among them, and
whisper-server on the GPU for the others and for "auto", with the model the settings choose
(voice_settings.model_for, loaded by voice/whisper-run).

Runs in Frametop's container (scripts/in-box: numpy, sherpa-onnx and pw-record are there),
named ft-voiced for pkill. Programs it starts for voice commands and hooks run on the host
(distrobox-host-exec), as the relay's commands do. Settings: voice_settings.py. Models:
~/.local/share/frametop/voice/models (voice/models.sh). Control socket for ft-voice:
/run/user/UID/frametop-voice/control.sock.
"""
